window.ScripturaLexicons.BDAG_PART_0288 = {"source":"BDAG","searchAnchorId":"bdag-search-anchor","entryAnchorId":"bdag-entry-anchor","rowsHtml":"<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-01\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλάξ, πλακός, ἡ substantivo feminino tábua; placa de pedra gravada BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλάξ, πλακός, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>tábua; placa de pedra gravada</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-02\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλάσις, εως, ἡ substantivo feminino formação; modelagem; criação BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλάσις, εως, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>formação; modelagem; criação</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-03\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλάσμα, ατος, τό substantivo neutro obra modelada; figura; criatura BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλάσμα, ατος, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>obra modelada; figura; criatura</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-04\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλάσσω verbo formar; modelar; moldar; formar o caráter BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλάσσω</td><td>verbo</td><td>formar; modelar; moldar; formar o caráter</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-05\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλαστός, ή, όν adjetivo fabricado; inventado; falso BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλαστός, ή, όν</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>fabricado; inventado; falso</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-06\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλατεῖα, ας, ἡ substantivo feminino rua; via larga BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλατεῖα, ας, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>rua; via larga</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-07\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλάτος, ους, τό substantivo neutro largura; extensão transversal; amplidão BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλάτος, ους, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>largura; extensão transversal; amplidão</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-08\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλατύνω verbo alargar; ampliar; abrir o coração BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλατύνω</td><td>verbo</td><td>alargar; ampliar; abrir o coração</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-09\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλατύς, εῖα, ύ adjetivo largo; amplo BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλατύς, εῖα, ύ</td><td>adjetivo</td><td>largo; amplo</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-10\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλατυσμός, οῦ, ὁ substantivo masculino alargamento; expansão; amplitude BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλατυσμός, οῦ, ὁ</td><td>substantivo masculino</td><td>alargamento; expansão; amplitude</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-11\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλέγμα, ατος, τό substantivo neutro trança; cabelo trançado BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλέγμα, ατος, τό</td><td>substantivo neutro</td><td>trança; cabelo trançado</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-12\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλείων, πλειόνως, πλεῖστος remissão gramatical ver πολύς BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλείων, πλειόνως, πλεῖστος</td><td>remissão gramatical</td><td>ver πολύς</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-13\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλέκω verbo entrelaçar; tecer; trançar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλέκω</td><td>verbo</td><td>entrelaçar; tecer; trançar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-14\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλέον remissão gramatical ver πολύς 1b e 2b BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλέον</td><td>remissão gramatical</td><td>ver πολύς 1b e 2b</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-15\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλεονάζω verbo aumentar; abundar; exceder; fazer aumentar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλεονάζω</td><td>verbo</td><td>aumentar; abundar; exceder; fazer aumentar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-16\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλεονεκτέω verbo explorar; defraudar; tirar vantagem; aumentar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλεονεκτέω</td><td>verbo</td><td>explorar; defraudar; tirar vantagem; aumentar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-17\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλεονέκτης, ου, ὁ substantivo masculino pessoa gananciosa; cobiçoso BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλεονέκτης, ου, ὁ</td><td>substantivo masculino</td><td>pessoa gananciosa; cobiçoso</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-18\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλεονεξία, ας, ἡ substantivo feminino ganância; avareza; cobiça insaciável BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλεονεξία, ας, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>ganância; avareza; cobiça insaciável</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-19\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλευρά, ᾶς, ἡ substantivo feminino lado; flanco; lado do corpo BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλευρά, ᾶς, ἡ</td><td>substantivo feminino</td><td>lado; flanco; lado do corpo</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"search-row\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" data-target=\"entry-bdag-0288-20\" data-source=\"BDAG\" data-search=\"πλέω verbo navegar; viajar por mar BDAG\" tabindex=\"0\"><td class=\"table-lemma greek\">πλέω</td><td>verbo</td><td>navegar; viajar por mar</td><td><span class=\"source-pill\">BDAG</span></td></tr>","cardsHtml":"<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-01\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλάξ, πλακός, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλάξ</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πλακός</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (Pind. e outros; inscrições, papiros, LXX, En, Test12Patr; ApcMos, prólogo), em geral, «algo que apresenta superfície plana»; em nossa literatura, pedra plana sobre a qual se podiam fazer inscrições, tábua, acerca das tábuas da lei (LXX; Philo, Migr. Abr. 85; Jos., Ant. 3, 90; SibOr 3, 257; sobre o costume de gravar em <span class=\"greek\">πλάκες</span> de pedra, veja Mitt-Wilck. I/2, 54, 1ss. [III a.C.]; OGI 672, 12) B 14:2 (cf. Ex 31:18; 34:4). <span class=\"greek\">πλάκες</span> <span class=\"greek\">λίθιναι</span> <span class=\"greek\">γεγραμμέναι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">δακτύλῳ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">χειρὸς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κυρίου</span> «tábuas de pedra escritas pelo dedo da mão do Senhor» B 4:7 (Ex 31:18). <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάκες</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">διαθήκης</span> «as tábuas da aliança» (<span class=\"greek\">διαθήκη</span> 3) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/HEB.9.4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hb 9:4</a>. Lançadas ao chão e quebradas em pedaços por Moisés (Ex 32:19; Dt 9:17), B 4:8; B 14:3. Paulo fala, tendo em mente Ex 32:16; 34:1 e aludindo a Ezk 11:19; 36:26, de uma <span class=\"greek\">ἐπιστολὴ</span> … <span class=\"greek\">ἐγγεγραμμένη</span> <span class=\"greek\">οὐκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλαξὶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">λιθίναις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀλλ</span>’ <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλαξὶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">καρδίαις</span> (a variante textual apresenta o mais fácil <span class=\"greek\">καρδίας</span>) <span class=\"greek\">σαρκίναις</span> «carta … escrita não em tábuas de pedra, mas em tábuas que são corações de carne» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.3.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 3:3</a> (cf. Theodor. Prod. 8, 353 Hercher <span class=\"greek\">ζωγραφεῖν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πρὸς</span> <span class=\"greek\">καρδίας</span> <span class=\"greek\">πινακίῳ</span>). Veja <span class=\"greek\">πλάτος</span>.—DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-02\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλάσις, εως, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλάσις</span>, <span class=\"greek\">εως</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλάσσω</span>; Theophr. e outros; papiros; ApcEsdr 2:23 p. 26, 16 Tdf. <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">σὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσιν</span>; Ath. 25:4 <span class=\"greek\">τῇ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κατὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσιν</span> <span class=\"greek\">διαθέσει</span>), ato de formar alguma coisa modelando uma substância maleável, formação, modelagem, criação (com genitivo, Polyb. 6, 53, 5; Plut., Cic. 862 [4, 4]; PSI 712, 5 <span class=\"greek\">πλάσις</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὀπτῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλίνθου</span>): <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἀδάμ</span> «a formação de Adão» B 6:9. <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀνθρώπων</span> «a criação dos seres humanos» AcPlCor 1:13. <span class=\"greek\">δευτέρα</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. «segunda criação», acerca da nova criação espiritual por meio de Cristo, B 6:13 (cf. Diod S 1, 16, 1).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πλάσσω</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-03\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλάσμα, ατος, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλάσμα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ατος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλάσσω</span>; Aristoph., Pla.+; PGM 4, 212; 304; 5, 378; LXX; En 104:10; TestSol 18:20; TestNapht 2:5; ApcSed; ApcMos 37; Philo; Jos., C. Ap. 1, 254; 2, 122; Just., D. 40, 1), aquilo que é formado ou modelado, imagem, figura: <span class=\"greek\">μὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐρεῖ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσμα</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσαντι</span>; «acaso aquilo que foi modelado dirá algo a quem o modelou?» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.9.20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 9:20</a> (Is 29:16; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.9.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 9:21</a> passa a mencionar <span class=\"greek\">κεραμεὺς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηλοῦ</span> «oleiro do barro»; cf. Aristoph., Av. 686 <span class=\"greek\">πλάσματα</span> <span class=\"greek\">πηλοῦ</span>). <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">παντοκράτωρ</span> … <span class=\"greek\">μὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">βουλόμενος</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀκυρῶσαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἴδιον</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσμα</span> «o Todo-Poderoso … não querendo estragar [ou invalidar] a sua própria obra» AcPlCor 2:12. O relato da criação (Gen 1:26) é interpretado em relação à regeneração, e os cristãos falam de si como <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">καλὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἡμῶν</span> «nossa bela criação» B 6:12. As palavras <span class=\"greek\">φθορεῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσματος</span> <span class=\"greek\">θεοῦ</span> «destruidores da obra de Deus» B 20:2 não precisam ser entendidas com esse pano de fundo; como mostra a passagem paralela D 5:2, derivam de outro complexo de ideias. Ao lado de <span class=\"greek\">φονεῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τέκνων</span> «assassinos de crianças», a expressão poderia significar aqueles que destroem o que Deus formou no ventre, pelo aborto (mas veja <span class=\"greek\">φθορεύς</span>).—M-M. TW. Sv.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-04\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλάσσω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλάσσω</span>, 1.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἔπλασα</span>; particípio perfeito <span class=\"greek\">πεπλακώς</span>. Passivo: 1.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλάσθην</span>; particípio perfeito neutro <span class=\"greek\">πεπλασμένον</span> LXX (veja as duas entradas anteriores; Hes. e outros; inscrições [por exemplo IAndrosIsis 94]; papiros, LXX; pseudoepígrafos; Philo; Jos., C. Ap. 1, 293; apologistas [Tat. 1, 1 <span class=\"greek\">πλάττειν</span>]).<br>① Produzir alguma coisa pela modelagem de uma substância maleável, formar, modelar.<br>ⓐ Sobre a fabricação de determinados objetos, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.9.20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 9:20</a> (veja <span class=\"greek\">πλάσμα</span>); Dg 2:3.<br>ⓑ Especialmente acerca da atividade criadora de Deus ao formar a humanidade (cf. Semonides de Amorgos 7, 21 sobre uma mulher, como objeto, <span class=\"greek\">πλάσαντες</span> <span class=\"greek\">γηίνην</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ὀλύμπιοι</span>; Babrius 66, 2s. <span class=\"greek\">πλάσσασθαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἄνθρωπον</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">γῆς</span>. Cf. Cornutus 18 p. 31, 20.—Artem. 3, 17 diz-se de Prometeu <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τοὺς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀνθρώπους</span>).<br><span class=\"greek\">α</span>. Sobre os primeiros pais, Adão e Eva (Gen 2:7s., 15; cf. 2 Macc 7:23; TestAbr B 8 p. 113, 4 [Stone p. 74]; Philo, Op. M. 137; Jos., Ant. 1, 32; SibOr 3, 24; Just., D. 19, 3 e outros): <span class=\"greek\">ἄνθρωπον</span> <span class=\"greek\">ταῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἱεραῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">χερσὶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔπλασεν</span> «[Deus] formou a humanidade com suas mãos santas» 1 Cl 33:4 (<span class=\"greek\">ἄρσεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θήλυ</span> no v. 5). Passivo: <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.2.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ti 2:13</a>, «Adão» e «Eva».<br><span class=\"greek\">β</span>. Sobre os seres humanos em geral, tendo em vista os primeiros pais: <span class=\"greek\">οὓς</span> (isto é, os humanos) <span class=\"greek\">ἐκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἰδίας</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἰκόνος</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔπλασεν</span> «aos quais [Deus] formou à sua própria imagem» Dg 10:2 (Himerius, Or. 64 [=Or. 18], 4: <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. sobre a formação de figuras por um escultor).<br><span class=\"greek\">γ</span>. Acerca da humanidade em geral, sem referência especial a Adão e Eva (frequentemente LXX; ApcEsdr 3:9 p. 27, 17 Tdf.; Ath. 31, 3), 1 Cl 38:3; B 19:2; AcPlCor 2:7. Especificamente, o coração humano foi formado por Deus, B 2:10 (cf. Ps 32:15).<br>② Dirigir a formação do caráter pessoal ou cultural, formar, moldar, em extensão figurada de 1: formação de coisas mentais na difícil passagem passiva <span class=\"greek\">δεῖξαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">αὐτῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">φῶς</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάσαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῇ</span> <span class=\"greek\">συνέσει</span> «mostrar-lhe luz e moldá-lo pelo entendimento (?)» 1 Cl 16:12 (Is 53:11 LXX, sem apoio no texto original tal como nos foi transmitido.—Quanto ao sentido figurado, cf. Pla., Rep. 377c <span class=\"greek\">πλάττειν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ψυχάς</span> [pela educação], Leg. 671c <span class=\"greek\">παιδεύειν</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάττειν</span>; Theocr. 7, 44).—B. 617. DELG. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-05\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλαστός, ή, όν</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλαστός</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ή</span>, <span class=\"greek\">όν</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλάσσω</span>; Hes. e outros), relativo ao que foi mentalmente construído sem fundamento factual, fabricado, inventado, falso (assim desde Eur., Bacch. 218; Hdt. 1, 68; Lycophron 432 <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλασταῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">γραφαῖς</span>; também PSI 494, 13 [III a.C.]; POxy 237 VIII, 14 [II d.C.]; Philo, Somn. 2, 140; Jos., Vi. 177; 337): <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">λόγοι</span> «palavras inventadas» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.2.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pt 2:3</a> (Ael. Aristid. 36, 91 K.=48 p. 474 D.: <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">λόγος</span> <span class=\"greek\">πέπλασται</span>; cf. POxy 237 VIII, 14 [II d.C.] acerca de um contrato falsificado).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πλάσσω</span>. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-06\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλατεῖα, ας, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλατεῖα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ας</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (propriamente feminino de <span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>, subentendendo-se <span class=\"greek\">ὁδός</span>: Sext. Emp., Pyrrh. 1, 188 <span class=\"greek\">ὅταν</span> <span class=\"greek\">λέγωμεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλατεῖαν</span>, <span class=\"greek\">δυνάμει</span> <span class=\"greek\">λέγομεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλατεῖαν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁδόν</span>), caminho largo, rua (Ps.-Eur., Rhes. 283; Diod S 12, 10, 7; 17, 52, 3; Plut., Dio 978 [46, 2], Thes. 27, 4; OGI 491, 9; inscrição lícia [Hauser 96]; papiros, LXX; TestAbr B 8 p. 113, 11s. [Stone p. 74]; Jos., Bell. 1, 425, Ant. 16, 148; Mel., P. 94, 724; empréstimo no rabínico), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.12.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 12:19</a> (Is 42:2); <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.6.56\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 6:56</a> D; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.10.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 10:10</a>; 13:26; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.5.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 5:15</a> (Maximus Tyr. 6, 2: as pessoas colocam seus doentes na rua para que os transeuntes lhes deem conselhos ou exerçam influência benéfica sobre eles); <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.11.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 11:8</a>; 21:21; 22:2. Com <span class=\"greek\">ῥύμη</span> (Tob 13:17, 18 BA; Is 15:3), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.14.21\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 14:21</a>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ταῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">γωνίαις</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. «nas esquinas das ruas» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.6.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 6:5</a>.—B. 720. DELG s.v. 1 <span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-07\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλάτος, ους, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλάτος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ους</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>; Hdt.+; inscrições, papiros, LXX; En 21:7; TestSol 11:8 C; TestAbr A 12 p. 91, 2 [Stone p. 30]; GrBar 11:8; EpArist; Philo; Jos., Bell. 7, 312, Ant. 8, 65, C. Ap. 2, 119.—<span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάτος</span> apenas por lapso em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.3.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eph 3:18</a> P46), extensão de um lado ao outro, largura, amplidão, com <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μῆκος</span> «comprimento» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.21.16\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 21:16a</a>, bem como com <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μῆκος</span> e <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὕψος</span> no v. 16b. Sobre <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάτος</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">μῆκος</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὕψος</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">βάθος</span> «a largura, o comprimento, a altura e a profundidade», <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.3.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eph 3:18</a>, veja <span class=\"greek\">βάθος</span> 1.—<span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάτος</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">γῆς</span> «a largura da terra» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.20.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 20:9</a> provém do OT (Da 12:2 LXX. Cf. Hab 1:6; Sir 1:3), mas o sentido não é claro: largura = a vasta planície terrestre talvez vise oferecer espaço aos incontáveis inimigos de Deus no v. 8, mas o movimento de «subir» combina melhor com Satanás (v. 7), recentemente solto e que novamente sobe do abismo (v. 3).—Em linguagem figurada (cf. Procop. Soph., Ep. 65; Nicetas Eugen. 2, 10 H. <span class=\"greek\">καρδίας</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλάτος</span>), <span class=\"greek\">τὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">δικαιώματα</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κυρίου</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλὰτη</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῆς</span> <span class=\"greek\">καρδίας</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑμῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐγέγραπτο</span> «os mandamentos do Senhor foram escritos de lado a lado em vosso coração» 1 Cl 2:8 (veja Pr 7:3; 22:20; 3:3 A; metáforas semelhantes em Aeschyl., Prom. 789; Soph., Fgm. 540 TGF; cf. o verbete <span class=\"greek\">πλάξ</span>.—Renehan ’75, 165).—DELG s.v. 1 <span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-08\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλατύνω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλατύνω</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>), aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλάτυνα</span> LXX. Passivo: 1.º futuro, 3.ª pessoa do singular <span class=\"greek\">πλατυνθήσεται</span> Gen 28:14; 1.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλατύνθην</span>; perfeito, 3.ª pessoa do singular <span class=\"greek\">πεπλάτυνται</span> (X. e outros; inscrições, LXX; TestSol 13:7 C; Jos., Ant. 9, 206; Ath., R. 19 p. 71, 24), fazer alguma coisa tornar-se larga, alargar, ampliar, literalmente, <span class=\"greek\">τὶ</span> «alguma coisa»: <span class=\"greek\">τὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">φυλακτήρια</span> «os filactérios» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.23.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 23:5</a> (veja <span class=\"greek\">φυλακτήριον</span>); <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.7.14\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 7:14</a>, variante textual (em lugar de <span class=\"greek\">ἔπλυναν</span>). Passivo (com <span class=\"greek\">παχύνεσθαι</span>; veja <span class=\"greek\">παχύνω</span> 1), ampliar-se, 1 Cl 3:1 (Dt 32:15).—Figuradamente, acerca da afeição calorosa: <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">καρδία</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡμῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πεπλάτυνται</span> «nosso coração está completamente aberto» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.6.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 6:11</a> (a expressão também ocorre em Dt 6:12, variante textual; 11:16; Ps 118:32. Cf. Epict., Fgm. Stob. 60 <span class=\"greek\">τὰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ψυχὰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">αὔξειν</span>); <span class=\"greek\">πλατύνθητε</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑμεῖς</span> «abri também vós amplamente vossos corações» v. 13; cf. SIG 783, 12.—DELG s.v. 1 <span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-09\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλατύς, εῖα, ύ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>adjetivo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>, <span class=\"greek\">εῖα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ύ</span> (veja as três entradas anteriores e a seguinte; Hom.+; inscrições, papiros, LXX, TestAbr; TestZeb 4:6, variante textual; JosAs, Philo, Joseph.; Mel., P. 45, 318; Ath., R. 19 p. 72, 9 [<span class=\"greek\">γέλως</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>]), relativo a grande extensão de um lado ao outro, largo, amplo, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.7.13\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 7:13</a>, acerca de um portão: <span class=\"greek\">πλατεῖα</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πύλη</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> … «larga é a porta e …» (leitura do texto; cf. Plut., Caes. 723 [33, 1] <span class=\"greek\">πλατεῖαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">πύλαι</span>; PFlor 333, 11 <span class=\"greek\">μέχρι</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλατείας</span> <span class=\"greek\">πύλης</span>; Jos., Bell. 3, 81); ou, acerca de um caminho, segundo a variante textual <span class=\"greek\">πλατεῖα</span> <span class=\"greek\">καὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">εὐρύχωρος</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁδός</span> «largo e espaçoso é o caminho» (cf. X., Cyr. 1, 6, 43 <span class=\"greek\">ἢ</span> <span class=\"greek\">στενὰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἢ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλατείας</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁδούς</span>; Arrian, Anab. 1, 1, 8 <span class=\"greek\">ὁδὸς</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλατεῖα</span>; SIG 57, 25 [V a.C.]; 313, 19s.; Jos., Bell. 6, 149).—B. 885. DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-10\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλατυσμός, οῦ, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλατυσμός</span>, <span class=\"greek\">οῦ</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>; Diosc. 5, 6 e outros; LXX; Philo, Somn. 2, 36).<br>① Estado de desenvolvimento crescente, extensão, alargamento, expansão (escólios sobre Pind.; Eustath., Prooem. 4), acerca de uma congregação (com <span class=\"greek\">δόξα</span>), 1 Cl 3:1.<br>② Estado do que é amplo, amplitude, extensão (2 Km 22:20; Ps 17:20; 118:45), em linguagem figurada acerca da paciência, que prospera por sua aplicação ampla, Hm 5, 2, 3 (<span class=\"greek\">εὐθηνέω</span> b).—DELG s.v. 1 <span class=\"greek\">πλατύς</span>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-11\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλέγμα, ατος, τό</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo neutro</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλέγμα</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ατος</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τό</span> (Eur., Pla., X.; Is 28:5 Aq. e Theod.; Philo; Jos., Ant. 2, 220: «algo entrelaçado ou tecido, trançado»), cabelo trançado, com ênfase em penteado elaborado, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TI.2.9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Ti 2:9</a>.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-12\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλείων, πλειόνως, πλεῖστος</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>remissão gramatical</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλείων</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πλειόνως</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πλεῖστος</span>: veja <span class=\"greek\">πολύς</span>.—M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-13\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλέκω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλέκω</span>, 1.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἔπλεξα</span>. Passivo: particípio aoristo <span class=\"greek\">πλακείς</span> Is 28:5; particípio perfeito <span class=\"greek\">πεπλεγμένος</span> (Hom. e outros; POsl 159, 10; 19 [III d.C.]; LXX; TestSol; JosAs cap. 11 cód. A [p. 53, linha 11 Bat.]; ApcrEzk [Epiph. 70, 10]; EpArist 70; Philo, Aet. M. 105; Jos., Ant. 3, 170), tecer, entrelaçar, trançar, <span class=\"greek\">στέφανον</span> «uma coroa» (Epici p. 23, Cypria Fgm. 4, 2 K.=Fgm. 5 p. 47 B.; Pind. e outros) <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.15.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 15:17</a>. <span class=\"greek\">τὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔκ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τινος</span> «alguma coisa com determinada matéria» (Alciphron 2, 35, 1; Paus. 2, 35, 5 <span class=\"greek\">στεφ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐκ</span>), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.27.29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 27:29</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.19.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 19:2</a>; passivo ApcPt 3:10.—B. 622. DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-14\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλέον</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>remissão gramatical</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλέον</span>: veja <span class=\"greek\">πολύς</span> 1b; 2b (<span class=\"greek\">πλείων</span>).</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-15\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλεονάζω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλεονάζω</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλέον</span>), futuro <span class=\"greek\">πλεονάσω</span> LXX; 1.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλεόνασα</span>; aoristo passivo, 3.ª pessoa do plural <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλεονάσθησαν</span> 1 Ch 5:23 (Thu., Hippocr. e outros; inscrições, papiros, LXX; PsSol 5:4; ApcEsdr 3:6 p. 27, 11 Tdf.; EpArist 295 [conjectura de Wendl.]; intransitivo em Thu. 1, 120, 4 e outros; no grego antigo, predominantemente em sentido negativo, referente a excesso).<br>① Tornar-se cada vez maior, de modo a existir em abundância, ser ou tornar-se mais, ser ou tornar-se grande, estar presente em abundância, crescer, aumentar, intransitivo (Strabo 4, 1, 13; Appian, Bell. Civ. 5, 89 §370; Ael. Aristid. 33 p. 616 D.; escólio sobre Nicander, Ther. 553; 2 Ch 24:11; Philo, Rer. Div. Her. 245; Jos., Ant. 19, 319), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.1.8\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pt 1:8</a>. Aumentar em número, multiplicar-se, Dg 6:9; cf. 7:8. Acerca do pecado (cf. Sir 23:3 <span class=\"greek\">ὅπως</span> <span class=\"greek\">μὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">αἱ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἁμαρτίαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">μου</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονάσωσι</span>), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.5.20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 5:20a</a> (cf. Philistion [IV a.C.] 4 p. 110, 8 Wellmann [veja Diocles] <span class=\"greek\">ἐπειδάν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονάσῃ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">θερμόν</span>), v. 20b. Acerca da graça, 6:1; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.4.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 4:15</a> (em notável violação do princípio helênico <span class=\"greek\">μηδὲν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἄγαν</span> «nada em excesso»). Acerca do amor, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2TH.1.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Th 1:3</a>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐπιζητῶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">καρπὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονάζοντα</span> «procuro o fruto que aumenta» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/PHP.4.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Phil 4:17</a>.<br>② Ter mais do que o necessário, ter em excesso, intransitivo (Diod S 2, 54, 7; 11, 59, 4; 19, 81, 3; Appian, Bell. Civ. 4, 108 §454, acerca de legiões com mais homens do que o número habitual), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.8.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 8:15</a> (Ex 16:18).<br>③ Ser responsável pelo aumento, transitivo.<br>ⓐ Produzir em abundância, aumentar, <span class=\"greek\">τὶ</span> «alguma coisa» (Ps 70:21; Jos., Ant. 1, 32): <span class=\"greek\">τὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">στόμα</span> <span class=\"greek\">σου</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλεόνασεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">κακίαν</span> «tua boca produziu maldade em abundância» 1 Cl 35:8 (Ps 49:19).<br>ⓑ Fazer aumentar (com <span class=\"greek\">περισσεύειν</span>): <span class=\"greek\">ὑμᾶς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">κύριος</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονάσαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῇ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀγάπῃ</span> «que o Senhor vos faça aumentar [isto é, enriquecer] em amor» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.3.12\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Th 3:12</a>.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">πλείων</span>. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-16\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλεονεκτέω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλεονεκτέω</span> (veja <span class=\"greek\">πλεονέκτης</span>), 1.º aoristo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλεονέκτησα</span>; passivo <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλεονεκτήθην</span> (desde Hdt. 8, 112; inscrições, papiros, LXX; Test12Patr; EpArist 270; Philo; Jos., Bell. 6, 79, Ant. 1, 66; 2, 260 e outros; Just., A I, 16, 4; predominantemente intransitivo, veja B-D-F §148, 1; Mlt. 65). Em nossa literatura, somente transitivo.<br>① Tirar vantagem de alguém, explorar, lograr, defraudar, enganar, <span class=\"greek\">τινά</span> «alguém» (Dionys. Hal. 9, 7; Dio Chrys. 67 [17], 8 <span class=\"greek\">τὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀδελφόν</span>; Plut., Marc. 315 [29, 7]; Ps.-Lucian, Amor. 27).<br>ⓐ Acerca de pessoas que exploram outras, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.7.2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 7:2</a> (com <span class=\"greek\">ἀδικεῖν</span> [cf. PCairMasp 151, 242s. <span class=\"greek\">ἀδικῶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεκτεῖσθαι</span>] e <span class=\"greek\">φθείρειν</span>); 12:18. <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τινὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">διά</span> <span class=\"greek\">τινος</span> «tirar vantagem de alguém por meio de outra pessoa» v. 17. <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τινὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῷ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πράγματι</span> «defraudar alguém no assunto» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.4.6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Th 4:6</a> (veja <span class=\"greek\">πρᾶγμα</span> 2).<br>ⓑ Acerca de Satanás, passivo (Demosth. 41, 25 <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεκτεῖσθαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">χιλίαις</span> <span class=\"greek\">δραχμαῖς</span>; OGI 484, 27 <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεκτεῖσθαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοὺς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὀλίγους</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑπ</span>’ <span class=\"greek\">αὐτῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀνθρώπους</span>): <span class=\"greek\">ἵνα</span> <span class=\"greek\">μὴ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεκτηθῶμεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὑπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοῦ</span> <span class=\"greek\">σατανᾶ</span> «para que não sejamos enganados por Satanás» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.2.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 2:11</a> («roubados» por Satanás de um membro de nosso grupo: BNoack, Satanas u. Soteria ’48, 98s.).<br>② Aumentar o número de alguma coisa, <span class=\"greek\">τὶ</span> «algo» (PCairMasp 3, 9 <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεκτῆσαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πράγματα</span>), acerca da lebre: <span class=\"greek\">κατ</span>’ <span class=\"greek\">ἐνιαυτὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀφόδευσιν</span> «aumentar anualmente a evacuação» B 10:6 (veja <span class=\"greek\">ἀφόδευσις</span>).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">ἔχω</span> e <span class=\"greek\">πλείων</span>. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-17\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλεονέκτης, ου, ὁ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo masculino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλεονέκτης</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ου</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> (=<span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλέον</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἔχων</span>; desde Hdt. [7, 158 como adjetivo]; PMagd 5, 7 [221 a.C.]; Sir 14:9; Philo, Mos. 1, 56; Ar. 10, 3; Just., A I, 12, 1), aquele que deseja possuir mais do que lhe cabe, pessoa gananciosa, cujas práticas são consideradas extremamente pecaminosas por cristãos e muitos outros. (Veja <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεξία</span> e JWeiss sobre <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.5.11\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Cor 5:11</a>. Na sociedade helênica, isso violava o princípio básico da proporção e contrariava a ideia de preocupação benéfica pelo conjunto dos cidadãos.) Entre os pecadores dos «dois caminhos», B 19:6; D 2:6. Também em outros lugares, com pessoas carregadas de vícios graves (como M. Ant. 11, 18, 6; Philo, Sacr. Abel. 32), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1CO.5.10\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Cor 5:10</a>s.; 6:10; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.5.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eph 5:5</a> (aqui caracterizado como <span class=\"greek\">εἰδωλολάτρης</span>; veja <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεξία</span>); Hs 6, 5, 5 (Thu. 1, 40, 1; X., Mem. 1, 2, 12 [ambos com <span class=\"greek\">βίαιος</span>]; 1, 5, 3, Cyr. 1, 6, 27 [com <span class=\"greek\">κλέπτης</span> e <span class=\"greek\">ἅρπαξ</span>]; Aristot., EN 5, 2 [com <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">παράνομος</span> e <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἄνισος</span>]; Diod S 20, 106, 4; Plut., Ages. 607 [20, 6] [com <span class=\"greek\">ἐν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ταῖς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐξουσίαις</span> <span class=\"greek\">πονηρός</span>], Mor. 57c [com <span class=\"greek\">κακοῦργος</span>]; Vett. Val. 42, 28 [com <span class=\"greek\">ἀλλοτρίων</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπιθυμητής</span>]).—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">ἔχω</span> e <span class=\"greek\">πλείων</span>. M-M. TW.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-18\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλεονεξία, ας, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλεονεξία</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ας</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (<span class=\"greek\">πλεονέκτης</span>), estado de desejar possuir mais do que é devido, ganância, insaciabilidade, avareza, cobiça (assim Hdt., Thu.+; Aristoxenus, Fgm. 50 p. 23, 36ss. [<span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. como vício puro e simples]; Diod S 21, 1, 4 [<span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. como <span class=\"greek\">μητρόπολις</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀδικημάτων</span>, «metrópole das injustiças»]; Musonius 72, 9; 90, 10 H.; Dio Chrys., Or. 67 [17] <span class=\"greek\">περί</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεξίας</span>: 6 <span class=\"greek\">μέγιστον</span> <span class=\"greek\">κακῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">αἴτιον</span>; 7 <span class=\"greek\">μέγιστον</span> <span class=\"greek\">κακόν</span>; Ael. Aristid. 39 p. 733 D.: <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. figura entre as três coisas mais vergonhosas; Herm. Wr. 13, 7; papiros, LXX; Test12Patr; GrBar 13:3; ApcMos 11; EpArist 277; Philo, Spec. Leg. 1, 173, Praem. 15 e outros; Jos., Bell. 7, 256, Ant. 3, 67; 7, 37 e outros; Just., D. 14, 2; Tat. 19, 2; Ath., R. 21 p. 74, 9; Theoph. Ant. 1, 14 [p. 92, 7]), B 10:4; com outros vícios (como Diod S 13, 30, 4 em catálogos de vícios; sobre eles, veja AVögtle, Die Tugend-u. Lasterkataloge im NT ’36), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ROM.1.29\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ro 1:29</a>; 1 Cl 35:5; B 20:1; D 5:1; Pol 2:2; Hm 6, 2, 5; 8:5. Com <span class=\"greek\">ἀκαθαρσία</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/EPH.4.19\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Eph 4:19</a>; 5:3. Caracterizada como <span class=\"greek\">εἰδωλολατρία</span> <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/COL.3.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Col 3:5</a> (veja <span class=\"greek\">εἰδωλολατρία</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πλεονέκτης</span> e cf. TestJud 19:1. Chaeremon, o estoico, mestre de Nero, em Porphyr., Abst. 4, 6 [=Chaeremon, Fgm. 10, p. 16 Horst], contrapõe <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεξία</span> a <span class=\"greek\">θεία</span> <span class=\"greek\">γνῶσις</span>). Acerca de falsos mestres, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2PE.2.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Pt 2:3</a>, 14 (veja <span class=\"greek\">γυμνάζω</span>, final).<br><span class=\"greek\">πρόφασις</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεξίας</span> (genitivo subjetivo) «pretexto para avareza» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/1TH.2.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">1 Th 2:5</a> (cf. Philostrat. I 362, 14 <span class=\"greek\">πρόσχημα</span> <span class=\"greek\">τ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">πλεονεξίας</span>). <span class=\"greek\">φυλάσσεσθαι</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἀπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πάσης</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. «guardar-se de toda forma de ganância» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.12.15\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 12:15</a>.—No plural, acerca das manifestações individuais de ganância (B-D-F §142.—X., Cyr. 1, 6, 29; Plut., Pomp. 640 [39, 6]; 2 Macc 4:50; Philo, Agr. 83, Vi. Cont. 70; Jos., Ant. 17, 253; Tat. 19, 2), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MRK.7.22\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mk 7:22</a>.—Em <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/2CO.9.5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2 Cor 9:5</a>, o contexto requer o sentido condensado «dádiva concedida de má vontade por avareza» (<span class=\"greek\">εὐλογία</span> 4); extorsão (Plummer, ICC, comentário sobre v. 10c).—WSedgwick, ET 36, 1925, 478s.; TManson, JTS 44, ’43, 86s.; EKlaar, <span class=\"greek\">Πλεονεξία</span>,-<span class=\"greek\">έκτης</span>,-<span class=\"greek\">εκτεῖν</span> TZ 10, ’54, 395–97.—DELG s.v. <span class=\"greek\">ἔχω</span> e <span class=\"greek\">πλείων</span>. M-M. TW. Spicq. Sv.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-19\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλευρά, ᾶς, ἡ</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>substantivo feminino</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλευρά</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ᾶς</span>, <span class=\"greek\">ἡ</span> (Hom.+), lado, principalmente do corpo humano, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/MAT.27.49\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mt 27:49</a>, variante textual; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/JHN.19.34\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">J 19:34</a> (sobre ambas as passagens, veja <span class=\"greek\">νύσσω</span> 1); 20:20, 25, 27; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.12.7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 12:7</a> (veja <span class=\"greek\">πατάσσω</span> 1a).—Acerca do lado plano de uma pedra, Hs 9, 4, 1.—B. 862. DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>\n<article class=\"entry-card\" id=\"entry-bdag-0288-20\" data-dictionary=\"grego\" hidden data-source=\"BDAG\"><header class=\"entry-header\"><div><h1 class=\"entry-title greek\">πλέω</h1><div class=\"entry-meta\"><span>verbo</span></div></div><div class=\"source-tag\">BDAG</div></header><div class=\"entry-divider\"></div><section class=\"entry-section\"><div class=\"section-title\">Tradução integral</div><p class=\"entry-text\"><span class=\"greek\">πλέω</span>, imperfeito, 1.ª pessoa do plural <span class=\"greek\">ἐπλέομεν</span>; futuro, 3.ª pessoa do singular <span class=\"greek\">πλευσεῖται</span> Ath. 22, 8; aoristo, 3.ª pessoa do singular <span class=\"greek\">ἔπλευσεν</span> 4 Macc 7:3 e Ath. 22:8; infinitivo <span class=\"greek\">πλεῦσαι</span> Jon 1:3 (Hom.+), viajar por mar, navegar, em uso absoluto (X., An. 5, 1, 4; Herodian 8, 2, 3), <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/LUK.8.23\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lk 8:23</a>; <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.27.24\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 27:24</a>; AcPl Ha 5, 16. Com o destino indicado (X., Hell. 1, 1, 8; Jos., Ant. 18, 111 <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ῥώμην</span>): <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">Συρίαν</span> «à Síria» <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/ACT.21.3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ac 21:3</a>. <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰταλίαν</span> «à Itália» 27:6. <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">τοὺς</span> <span class=\"greek\">κατὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τὴν</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἀσίαν</span> <span class=\"greek\">τόπους</span> «aos lugares da Ásia» v. 2. Com o ponto de partida e o destino (Appian, Liby. 113 §535 <span class=\"greek\">ἀπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Σικελίας</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐς</span> <span class=\"greek\">Ἰτύκην</span> [Útica]): <span class=\"greek\">ἀπὸ</span> <span class=\"greek\">Τρῳάδος</span> <span class=\"greek\">εἰς</span> <span class=\"greek\">Νεάπολιν</span> «de Trôade a Neápolis» IPol 8:1.—Substantivado: <span class=\"greek\">πᾶς</span> <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τόπον</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλέων</span> «todo aquele que navega para algum lugar» = «marítimo, viajante por mar» (provavelmente referência a turistas que viajam para visitar as atrações da «Babilônia» [sobre turismo no mundo romano, veja LFriedländer, Roman Life and Manners under the Early Empire7, tradução de LMagnus, 1907, I 323–94]). Estes são mencionados ao lado de marinheiros e mercadores, <a class=\"reference reference-link\" href=\"https://www.die-bibel.de/en/bible/NA28/REV.18.17\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rv 18:17</a>. As variantes textuais (<span class=\"greek\">τὸν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ποταμόν</span>, <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλοίων</span>, <span class=\"greek\">πόντον</span> [sobre os problemas textuais, veja RBorger, TRu 52, ’87, 51–53]) levaram a diversas interpretações. Alguns traduzem «todos os que navegam ao longo da costa» (deWette, HHoltzmann, Bousset, Lohmeyer e outros; quanto a <span class=\"greek\">πλ</span>. <span class=\"greek\">ἐπί</span> com acusativo de lugar, veja Thu. 1, 53, 2; 4 Macc 7:3. Em FPhGr I 489, 28 temos <span class=\"greek\">πλέοντες</span> <span class=\"greek\">παρὰ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τόπον</span>. Sobre a variante textual <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλοίων</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλέων</span>, cf. Lucian, Ver. Hist. 1, 34; SIG 409, 5s. <span class=\"greek\">ἔπλευσεν</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">τῶν</span> <span class=\"greek\">νεῶν</span>. O manuscrito 469 apresenta <span class=\"greek\">ἐπὶ</span> <span class=\"greek\">πόντον</span>, apoiado parcialmente pelo «super mare» de Primasius. Veja EbNestle, Einführung in das Griech. NT 1909, 182; AFridrichsen, K. Hum. Vetensk.-Samf. i Upps. Årsb. ’43, 31, nota: <span class=\"greek\">ὁ</span> <span class=\"greek\">ἐπίτοπον</span> <span class=\"greek\">πλέων</span> = «aquele que navega ocasionalmente, passageiro». Veja também IHeikel, StKr 106, ’34/35, 317).—LCasson, Travel in the Ancient World ’74. B. 680s. DELG. M-M.</p></section></article>"};
